      "text": "To solve for \\( x \\) in the given diagram, we need to use the fact that the angles around a point sum up to \\( 360^\\circ \\).\n\nFirst, let's identify the angles around the center of the circle. We have four angles labeled as follows:\n- \\( 4x^\\circ \\)\n- \\( 5x^\\circ \\)\n- \\( 2x^\\circ \\)\n- \\( x^\\circ \\)\n\nThe angles around the center of the circle must sum up to \\( 360^\\circ \\). Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\n\\[\n4x + 5x + 2x + x = 360^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the terms on the left side of the equation:\n\n\\[\n4x + 5x + 2x + x = 12x\n\\]\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\n12x = 360^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 12:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{360^\\circ}{12} = 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30}\n\\]",
