      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) in the given diagram, we need to use the fact that the sum of the angles around a point is \\( 360^\\circ \\). The angles given in the diagram are \\( 4x^\\circ \\), \\( 5x^\\circ \\), \\( 2x^\\circ \\), and \\( x^\\circ \\). The point where these angles meet is the center of the circle, so the sum of these angles must be \\( 360^\\circ \\).\n\nWe can set up the following equation:\n\n\\[ 4x + 5x + 2x + x = 360^\\circ \\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[ 12x = 360^\\circ \\]\n\nDividing both sides by 12, we find:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{360^\\circ}{12} = 30^\\circ \\]\n\nLet's verify this by coding the solution in Python.\n```python\n# Calculate the value of x\nx = 360 / 12\nprint(x)\n```\n```output\n30.0\n```\nThe value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{30}\\).",
